# Which skills get a directory in .claude/skills/ — and therefore a slot in every
# session's start-up roster.
#
# Everything NOT listed here is either in .claude/skill-library/ (tier 2, indexed
# on demand by the `skill-library` skill) or deleted outright. Deletion is for
# skills that teach general craft the model already has; archiving is for
# specialist content that is real but rarely needed.
#
# THE BUDGET IS CHARACTERS, NOT ENTRIES.
#
# Claude Code concatenates every skill's name and description into the session
# roster and truncates that string when it overflows — it does not drop whole
# entries, it stops mid-word, and every entry after the cut arrives as a bare
# slug. A skill whose description never reaches the model cannot be
# auto-invoked, so it costs a line and buys nothing.
#
# This was measured, not guessed. With 81 entries totalling 26,629 chars the
# roster truncated around position 73 of 81: `scrutinize` (505 ch),
# `system-design` (700 ch) and six others arrived bare, while `tdd` at position
# 78 survived purely because its description was 75 chars and still fit. That is
# a greedy byte-fill hitting a ceiling, which sits somewhere near 21,000 chars.
#
# So "90 entries" was the wrong control variable — a roster of 90 short
# descriptions fits comfortably while 81 long ones did not. Budget the sum of
# description lengths and keep it under ~18,000 chars for margin.
#
# The bar for tier 1:
#
#   1. facts about THIS repo, machine or fleet that cannot be inferred
#   2. version-specific API surface that is easy to misremember
#      (Effect, MikroORM v7, Next 16, Logto)
#   3. the workflow rails — ID, Maestro, tooling contracts
#   4. anything a .claude/commands/*.md invokes by name
#
# What does NOT belong, at any description length: general software craft the
# model performs natively. Commit conventions, rebasing, merge resolution, ADR
# format, clean/hexagonal architecture, DDD theory, generic React guidance,
# generic Playwright guidance, design taste. Those were deleted in full — the
# roster is for things the model cannot derive, not lessons it does not need.
#
#   bash .claude/bin/sync-skills.sh          apply
#   bash .claude/bin/sync-skills.sh --check  verify

